#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""g16-idlemask-bisect: which devices hold the G16's not-idle idlemask bits (#249).

amd_pmc's idlemask (debugfs amd_pmc/amd_pmc_idlemask) sits at 0xffce9add on the G16
at idle: bits 1, 5, 8, 10, 13, 14, 16, 20 and 21 read 0, not idle. This kit takes the
removable PCI devices off the bus (sysfs remove) in halves and reads the idlemask at
10 Hz after each change, so each bit ends up with the device, or the devices together,
holding it. A bit that stays not idle with every removable device gone, the screen off
and the apps frozen is either waiting for a quieter machine or held by firmware: the
question for AMD (drm/amd#5863).

  g16-idlemask-bisect               run it (one root prompt, then hands off; 6-11 min)
  g16-idlemask-bisect --list        the removable groups found, the preflight, nothing changed
  g16-idlemask-bisect --dry-run     change nothing, simulate the devices and bits (no root)
  g16-idlemask-bisect --post        post the report to #249 with bin/issue at the end
  options: --settle S (3) --settle-rescan S (5) --measure S (3)       pass 1 phases
           --watts-settle S (10) --watts-measure S (30)               pass 2 phases
           --quiet S (60)                                             the quiet phase
           --skip a,b --only a,b --no-screen --no-follow --out DIR --sim MODEL.json (dry run)

Groups (found at run time by driver, class and vendor; the BDFs are the G16's):
  rtx        the RTX's root port (00:03.1) and everything behind it; skipped while
             anything holds the RTX's DRM node or /dev/nvidia* (Hyprland does on the
             G16: removing it there would take the compositor down)
  wifi       mt7925e (63:00.0)            sd        GL9767 SD reader (62:00.0)
  usb4       the USB4 NHI (67:00.5)       xhci-kbd  the xHCI with the keyboard (USB
  xhci-cam   the xHCI with the camera               0b05:19b6) and Bluetooth (67:00.0)
             (65:00.4)                    xhci-*    each other xHCI (67:00.3, 67:00.4)
  audio      the SoC's HDA (65:00.6)      hdmi-audio  the AMD GPU's HDMI audio (65:00.1)
  acp        the audio coprocessor (65:00.5)          npu  the NPU, amdxdna (66:00.1)
  psp        ccp/PSP (65:00.2)            smbus     piix4 SMBus (00:14.0): its driver is
                                                    unbound instead (on the root bus, a
                                                    rescan would reach the RTX's port)
  Never: the NVMe (the root disk), the AMD GPU, bridges and host bridges, anything
  without a driver. A group whose camera or NPU node is open is skipped. Only the
  removed device's own bus is rescanned, with its port held awake; the global rescan is
  a fallback for a device that doesn't come back.

Pass 1, the bits (short phases: 3 s settle, 5 s after a rescan, then 3 s of reads at
10 Hz; a bit counts as not idle at >= 80 % of reads, idle at <= 20 %):
  baseline; everything off (the first split). If no bit goes idle there, the bisect is
  skipped. Otherwise: for a set whose removal lets bits go idle, remove half A, then
  half B, and recurse into each half for the bits that went idle there (both halves
  when they free different bits). A bit that goes idle with the whole set off but with
  neither half alone needs devices from both: it is bisected in B with A off and in A
  with B off, and reported as "needs X + Y together". Then the screen off (DPMS, through
  hyprctl) with everything on, and with everything off.
  The quiet phase, held 60 s: every removable device off, the screen off and the app
  scopes frozen (cgroup freezer, app.slice scopes only: never services, the compositor,
  the shell, audio or polkit) all at once, with the wakeups/s (/proc/interrupts), the
  deepest cpuidle state's residency, gpu_metrics and the display -> SMU probes (the
  DCN's SMU messages, Z-state decisions, idle-optimization allows and DML
  StutterPeriod). A bit that goes idle only here wants a quieter machine; one still
  stuck is firmware. The report says which.
Pass 2, the watts (10 s settle + 30 s measured): baseline, everything off, each device
  or device set pass 1 tied to a bit (its idlemask confirms pass 1), and the baseline
  again; each against the mean of the two baselines. Battery watts are BAT current_now x
  voltage_now every second; socket power is gpu_metrics' average_socket_power (struct
  gpu_metrics_v3_0, natural alignment: offset 112) every 0.5 s.

Preflight (it refuses and changes nothing if any holds): on AC or not discharging;
the GPU MUX not in hybrid mode (asus-armoury gpu_mux_mode must be 1: the internal
panel on the AMD GPU); an external display connected (HDMI or DP); the RTX not
runtime-suspended or its video memory awake (/proc/driver/nvidia). The RTX is never
woken to check: only its runtime_status and /proc/driver/nvidia are read, never
nvidia-smi, sensors, its config space or the nvidia_0 backlight.

Root: one pkexec prompt at the start, through the desktop's polkit agent
(G16_POLKIT_REASON=<wrapper> runs `<wrapper> run REASON -- pkexec ...` for a dialog
with a reason; G16_ROOT=sudo is the other way). g16-testd (#277) can't remove PCI
devices, freeze scopes or load these probes (its allowlist has the SD reader), so it
isn't used. The run itself is a root transient unit (g16-idlemask-bisect-run), outside
app.slice so the freezer never reaches it, and it carries on when the keyboard,
touchpad, Wi-Fi and the terminal drop out; this command follows its log.

Restore: on exit, error or signal it thaws the apps, removes the probes, turns the
screen back on, rescans the removed devices' buses, re-binds any driver that didn't
come back and puts the keyboard light back. A watchdog unit
(g16-idlemask-bisect-watchdog-*) does the same if the run dies, or stops it after 25
minutes. If anything is still missing afterwards, a reboot brings every device back:
nothing here persists across a reboot. After the psp group, amd-pmf's policy session
may stay stale until the next boot.

Output: ~/omarchy-asus-249-bisect/ (report.md, bisect.json with every phase's reads,
run.log). The report is written to be posted on #249 as it is; --post does that
through bin/issue next to this script (its personal-information scan applies).

Exit status: 0 when the run finished, 1 on a refusal or a problem, 2 on bad usage.
"""
import argparse
import glob
import json
import os
import pwd
import random
import re
import signal
import stat
import statistics
import struct
import subprocess
import sys
import threading
import time

SYS = os.environ.get("G16_BISECT_SYS", "/sys")  # overrides for the offline tests only
PROC = os.environ.get("G16_BISECT_PROC", "/proc")
ISSUE = 249
SELF = os.path.realpath(__file__)
UNIT_USER, UNIT_RUN, UNIT_WATCHDOG = "g16-idlemask-bisect", "g16-idlemask-bisect-run", "g16-idlemask-bisect-watchdog"
BDF_RE = re.compile(r"^[0-9a-f]{4}:[0-9a-f]{2}:[0-9a-f]{2}\.[0-7]$")
STUCK, IDLE = 0.8, 0.2       # share of reads with the bit not idle
DEADLINE_S = 25 * 60
# Estimated costs for the dry run's time estimate (seconds).
T_REMOVE, T_RESCAN, T_DPMS, T_START, T_END = 1.0, 5.0, 1.5, 40.0, 20.0


def rd(p, d=None, n=4096):
    try:
        with open(p, errors="replace") as f:
            return f.read(n).strip()
    except OSError:
        return d


def wr(p, v):
    try:
        with open(p, "w") as f:
            f.write(str(v) + "\n")
        return True
    except OSError:
        return False


LOGF = None


def log(*a):
    line = time.strftime("%H:%M:%S ") + " ".join(str(x) for x in a)
    try:
        print(line, flush=True)
    except OSError:
        pass
    if LOGF:
        try:
            with open(LOGF, "a") as f:
                f.write(line + "\n")
        except OSError:
            pass


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the idlemask
def parse_mask(text):
    """The idlemask's value from the debugfs file (it may carry a label)."""
    m = re.search(r"0x[0-9a-fA-F]+", text or "")
    return int(m.group(0), 16) if m else None


def not_idle_bits(mask, width=32):
    """Bits that read 0: not idle."""
    return [b for b in range(width) if not (mask >> b) & 1]


def bit_shares(masks, width=32):
    """bit -> share of the reads with it not idle (reads that failed are left out)."""
    good = [m for m in masks if m is not None]
    if not good:
        return {}
    return {b: sum(1 for m in good if not (m >> b) & 1) / len(good) for b in range(width)}


# ----------------------------------------------------------------- gpu_metrics
# struct gpu_metrics_v3_0 (drivers/gpu/drm/amd/include/kgd_pp_interface.h), up to
# average_all_core_power, with C natural alignment: 264 bytes in all.
GM_V3_0 = [
    ("structure_size", "H", 1), ("format_revision", "B", 1), ("content_revision", "B", 1),
    ("temperature_gfx", "H", 1), ("temperature_soc", "H", 1), ("temperature_core", "H", 16),
    ("temperature_skin", "H", 1), ("average_gfx_activity", "H", 1), ("average_vcn_activity", "H", 1),
    ("average_ipu_activity", "H", 8), ("average_core_c0_activity", "H", 16),
    ("average_dram_reads", "H", 1), ("average_dram_writes", "H", 1),
    ("average_ipu_reads", "H", 1), ("average_ipu_writes", "H", 1),
    ("system_clock_counter", "Q", 1),
    ("average_socket_power", "I", 1), ("average_ipu_power", "H", 1), ("average_apu_power", "I", 1),
    ("average_gfx_power", "I", 1), ("average_dgpu_power", "I", 1), ("average_all_core_power", "I", 1),
    ("average_core_power", "H", 16), ("average_sys_power", "H", 1),
    ("stapm_power_limit", "H", 1), ("current_stapm_power_limit", "H", 1),
    ("average_gfxclk_frequency", "H", 1), ("average_socclk_frequency", "H", 1),
    ("average_vpeclk_frequency", "H", 1), ("average_ipuclk_frequency", "H", 1),
    ("average_fclk_frequency", "H", 1), ("average_vclk_frequency", "H", 1),
    ("average_uclk_frequency", "H", 1), ("average_mpipu_frequency", "H", 1),
    ("current_coreclk", "H", 16), ("current_core_maxfreq", "H", 1), ("current_gfx_maxfreq", "H", 1),
    ("throttle_residency_prochot", "I", 1), ("throttle_residency_spl", "I", 1),
    ("throttle_residency_fppt", "I", 1), ("throttle_residency_sppt", "I", 1),
    ("throttle_residency_thm_core", "I", 1), ("throttle_residency_thm_gfx", "I", 1),
    ("throttle_residency_thm_soc", "I", 1), ("time_filter_alphavalue", "I", 1),
]


def layout(fields):
    """name -> (offset, struct code); and the size, padded to the largest alignment."""
    off, out, big = 0, {}, 1
    for name, code, n in fields:
        sz = struct.calcsize("<" + code)
        big = max(big, sz)
        off = (off + sz - 1) // sz * sz
        out[name] = (off, code, n)
        off += sz * n
    return out, (off + big - 1) // big * big


GM_LAYOUT, GM_SIZE = layout(GM_V3_0)
GM_POWER = {"socket_mw": "average_socket_power", "ipu_mw": "average_ipu_power", "apu_mw": "average_apu_power",
            "gfx_mw": "average_gfx_power", "dgpu_mw": "average_dgpu_power", "core_mw": "average_all_core_power"}


def parse_gpu_metrics(b):
    """The power fields (mW) and the clock counter of a v3.0 table; None for another format.
    0xffff / 0xffffffff (not reported) come back as None."""
    if len(b) < 4:
        return None
    size, fmt, content = struct.unpack_from("<HBB", b, 0)
    if fmt != 3 or content != 0 or len(b) < GM_LAYOUT["average_all_core_power"][0] + 4:
        return None
    out = {"size": size}
    off, code, _ = GM_LAYOUT["system_clock_counter"]
    out["clock_counter"] = struct.unpack_from("<" + code, b, off)[0]
    for k, name in GM_POWER.items():
        off, code, _ = GM_LAYOUT[name]
        v = struct.unpack_from("<" + code, b, off)[0]
        out[k] = None if v == (0xFFFF if code == "H" else 0xFFFFFFFF) else v
    return out


# ------------------------------------------------------------------ discovery
def pci_devices():
    out = {}
    for p in sorted(glob.glob(SYS + "/bus/pci/devices/*")):
        bdf = os.path.basename(p)
        real = os.path.realpath(p)
        parent = os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(real))
        drv = os.path.basename(os.path.realpath(p + "/driver")) if os.path.lexists(p + "/driver") else ""
        out[bdf] = {"bdf": bdf, "vendor": rd(p + "/vendor", ""), "device": rd(p + "/device", ""),
                    "cls": rd(p + "/class", ""), "driver": drv, "path": real,
                    "parent": parent if BDF_RE.match(parent) else ""}
    return out


def below(devs, top):
    base = devs[top]["path"] + "/"
    return [b for b in sorted(devs) if devs[b]["path"].startswith(base)]


def usb_below(pci_path):
    """USB devices below a PCI device: (vendor:product, interface classes)."""
    out = []
    for u in sorted(glob.glob(SYS + "/bus/usb/devices/*")):
        if not os.path.exists(u + "/idVendor") or not os.path.realpath(u).startswith(pci_path + "/"):
            continue
        vid, pid = rd(u + "/idVendor", ""), rd(u + "/idProduct", "")
        if vid == "1d6b":  # the root hubs
            continue
        ifc = {rd(i + "/bInterfaceClass", "") for i in glob.glob(os.path.realpath(u) + "/*:*")}
        out.append((f"{vid}:{pid}", ifc))
    return out


def root_disk_bdfs():
    """PCI devices on the path of the block device holding / (never touched)."""
    out = set()
    for line in (rd(PROC + "/self/mountinfo", "", 1 << 20) or "").splitlines():
        f = line.split()
        if len(f) > 4 and f[4] == "/":
            p = os.path.realpath(f"{SYS}/dev/block/{f[2]}")
            out.update(x for x in p.split("/") if BDF_RE.match(x))
    return out


KBD_USB = "0b05:19b6"


def classify(d, devs):
    """(group kind, label) for a device, or (None, why it is left alone)."""
    c, v, drv = d["cls"][2:6], d["vendor"], d["driver"]
    if c.startswith("06"):
        return None, "bridge"
    if c.startswith("01"):
        return None, "storage (the NVMe)"
    if drv == "amdgpu" or (v == "0x1002" and c.startswith("03")):
        return None, "the AMD GPU"
    if v == "0x10de":
        return None, "behind the RTX's port (the rtx group)"
    if not drv:
        return None, "no driver"
    if drv == "mt7925e" or c == "0280":
        return "wifi", f"Wi-Fi ({drv})"
    if c == "0805" or (v, d["device"]) == ("0x17a0", "0x9767"):
        return "sd", f"SD reader ({drv})"
    if drv == "thunderbolt" or d["cls"] == "0x0c0340":
        return "usb4", "USB4 NHI (thunderbolt)"
    if d["cls"] == "0x0c0330":
        usb = usb_below(d["path"])
        ids = ", ".join(i for i, _ in usb)
        if any(i == KBD_USB for i, _ in usb):
            bt = [i for i, ifc in usb if "e0" in ifc]
            return "xhci-kbd", f"xHCI with the keyboard ({KBD_USB})" + (f" and Bluetooth ({', '.join(bt)})" if bt else "")
        cam = [i for i, ifc in usb if "0e" in ifc]
        if cam:
            return "xhci-cam", f"xHCI with the camera ({', '.join(cam)})"
        return "xhci", "xHCI" + (f" ({ids})" if ids else " (nothing plugged in)")
    if c == "0403":
        if v == "0x1002":
            return "hdmi-audio", f"the AMD GPU's HDMI audio ({drv})"
        return "audio", f"HDA ({drv})"
    if drv.startswith("snd_acp") or (c == "0480" and v == "0x1022"):
        return "acp", f"audio coprocessor ({drv})"
    if drv == "amdxdna" or c == "1180":
        return "npu", f"NPU ({drv})"
    if drv == "ccp" or c == "1080":
        return "psp", f"PSP ({drv})"
    if c == "0c05":
        return "smbus", f"SMBus ({drv})"
    return None, f"not a removable kind ({drv})"


def discover(devs=None):
    """The removable groups (by address) and the devices left alone, with why."""
    devs = pci_devices() if devs is None else devs
    disk = root_disk_bdfs()
    groups, left, used = [], {}, set()

    def add(name, label, top):
        members = [top] + below(devs, top)
        if disk & set(members):
            left[top] = "on the root disk's path"
            return
        used.update(members)
        bus = top.rsplit(":", 1)[0]
        # On the root bus (the SMBus) the driver is unbound instead: getting it back would
        # take a rescan of the root bus, which reads the RTX's port and probes behind it.
        method = "unbind" if not devs[top]["parent"] and name != "rtx" else "remove"
        groups.append({"name": name, "label": label + (" (driver unbound, not removed)" if method == "unbind" else ""),
                       "top": top, "members": members, "drivers": {m: devs[m]["driver"] for m in members},
                       "port": devs[top]["parent"], "bus": bus, "method": method})

    rtx = next((d for d in devs.values() if d["vendor"] == "0x10de" and d["cls"].startswith("0x03")), None)
    if rtx and rtx["parent"] and devs.get(rtx["parent"], {}).get("cls", "").startswith("0x0604"):
        add("rtx", "the RTX's root port and everything behind it", rtx["parent"])
    for bdf, d in sorted(devs.items()):
        if bdf in used:
            continue
        kind, why = classify(d, devs)
        if kind is None:
            left[bdf] = why
            continue
        name = kind if kind != "xhci" else "xhci-" + bdf[5:]
        if any(g["name"] == name for g in groups):
            name = f"{kind}-{bdf[5:]}"
        add(name, why, bdf)
    # By address: functions of one bus (one USB4 complex, the GPU's audio blocks) sit
    # together, so a bit they share is less often split between the bisect's halves.
    groups.sort(key=lambda g: g["top"])
    return groups, left


# ------------------------------------------------------------------ preflight
def find_rtx(devs):
    return next((b for b, d in sorted(devs.items()) if d["vendor"] == "0x10de" and d["cls"].startswith("0x03")), None)


def battery():
    for s in sorted(glob.glob(SYS + "/class/power_supply/*")):
        if rd(s + "/type") == "Battery" and rd(s + "/scope") != "Device":
            return s
    return None


def bat_w(bat):
    """Battery watts: current_now x voltage_now, else power_now."""
    if not bat:
        return None
    c, v = rd(bat + "/current_now"), rd(bat + "/voltage_now")
    if c and v and c.lstrip("-").isdigit() and v.isdigit() and int(c) != 0:
        return abs(int(c)) * int(v) / 1e12
    p = rd(bat + "/power_now")
    if p and p.lstrip("-").isdigit():
        return abs(int(p)) / 1e6
    return None


def mux_mode():
    for p in sorted(glob.glob(SYS + "/class/firmware-attributes/*/attributes/gpu_mux_mode/current_value")) + \
            [SYS + "/devices/platform/asus-nb-wmi/gpu_mux_mode"]:
        v = rd(p)
        if v is not None:
            return v
    return None


def card_driver(card):
    return os.path.basename(os.path.realpath(f"{SYS}/class/drm/{card}/device/driver"))


def preflight(devs, as_root=False):
    """(refusals, facts). Reads only cached sysfs and /proc/driver/nvidia."""
    bad, facts = [], {}
    prod = (rd(SYS + "/class/dmi/id/product_name", "") or "") + " " + (rd(SYS + "/class/dmi/id/board_name", "") or "")
    facts["machine"] = prod.strip()
    if "GA605" not in prod:
        bad.append(f"this is not a ROG Zephyrus G16 GA605 ({prod.strip() or 'unknown'})")
    for s in sorted(glob.glob(SYS + "/class/power_supply/*")):
        if rd(s + "/type") in ("Mains", "USB", "USB_C", "USB_PD") and rd(s + "/online") == "1":
            bad.append(f"on AC ({os.path.basename(s)} online): unplug the charger, it must run on battery")
    bat = battery()
    st = rd(bat + "/status") if bat else None
    facts["battery"] = f"{st}, {rd(bat + '/capacity', '?')} %" if bat else "none"
    if not bat:
        bad.append("no battery found")
    elif st != "Discharging":
        bad.append(f"the battery is not discharging ({st}): unplug the charger")
    mux = mux_mode()
    facts["gpu_mux_mode"] = mux
    if mux is None:
        bad.append("can't read the GPU MUX mode (asus-armoury gpu_mux_mode)")
    elif mux != "1":
        bad.append(f"the GPU MUX is not in hybrid mode (gpu_mux_mode={mux}): the internal panel must be on the AMD GPU")
    for c in sorted(glob.glob(SYS + "/class/drm/card*-*")):
        n = os.path.basename(c)
        conn = n.split("-", 1)[1]
        if rd(c + "/status") != "connected":
            continue
        if conn.startswith("eDP"):
            drv = card_driver(n.split("-", 1)[0])
            facts["panel"] = f"{conn} on {drv}"
            if drv != "amdgpu":
                bad.append(f"the internal panel ({conn}) is driven by {drv}, not the AMD GPU")
        elif conn.startswith(("HDMI", "DP", "DVI")):
            bad.append(f"an external display is connected ({conn}): unplug it")
    rtx = find_rtx(devs)
    if rtx:
        rs = rd(f"{SYS}/bus/pci/devices/{rtx}/power/runtime_status", "?")
        facts["rtx"] = rs
        if rs != "suspended":
            bad.append(f"the RTX is {rs}, not runtime-suspended: close what uses it (an external display, a game) and wait")
        pw = rd(f"{PROC}/driver/nvidia/gpus/{rtx}/power", "", 4096) or ""
        m = re.search(r"Video Memory:\s*(\S+)", pw)
        if m:
            facts["rtx_video_memory"] = m.group(1)
            if m.group(1) != "Off":
                bad.append(f"the RTX's video memory is {m.group(1)} (/proc/driver/nvidia): something is running on it")
    if as_root and parse_mask(rd(SYS + "/kernel/debug/amd_pmc/amd_pmc_idlemask", "", 200)) is None:
        bad.append("can't read amd_pmc_idlemask (debugfs, amd_pmc)")
    return bad, facts


# ------------------------------------------------------- open device nodes
def open_char_devs():
    """(major, minor) -> ["comm[pid]", ...] for every open character device; plus /dev/nvidia* holders."""
    out, nv = {}, []
    for p in glob.glob(PROC + "/[0-9]*"):
        comm = rd(p + "/comm", "?")
        try:
            fds = os.listdir(p + "/fd")
        except OSError:
            continue
        for fd in fds:
            f = f"{p}/fd/{fd}"
            try:
                tgt = os.readlink(f)
                if not tgt.startswith("/dev/"):
                    continue
                s = os.stat(f)
            except OSError:
                continue
            if stat.S_ISCHR(s.st_mode):
                out.setdefault((os.major(s.st_rdev), os.minor(s.st_rdev)), set()).add(f"{comm}[{os.path.basename(p)}]")
                if tgt.startswith("/dev/nvidia"):
                    nv.append(f"{comm} {tgt}")
    return out, sorted(set(nv))


def group_nodes(g, devs):
    """(major, minor, name) of the DRM, video and accel nodes below a group (sysfs dev files only)."""
    out = []
    for m in g["members"]:
        top = devs.get(m, {}).get("path")
        if not top:
            continue
        for root, dirs, files in os.walk(top):
            dirs[:] = [d for d in dirs if "backlight" not in d and not d.startswith("nvidia_")]
            if os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(root)) in ("drm", "video4linux", "accel") and "dev" in files:
                v = rd(root + "/dev", "")
                if re.match(r"^\d+:\d+$", v):
                    a, b = v.split(":")
                    out.append((int(a), int(b), os.path.basename(root)))
    return out


def busy_groups(groups, devs):
    """name -> why it can't be removed now (a holder of its DRM, camera or NPU node)."""
    held, nv = open_char_devs()
    out = {}
    for g in groups:
        who = []
        for a, b, n in group_nodes(g, devs):
            for h in sorted(held.get((a, b), ())):
                who.append(f"{h} has {n} open")
        if g["name"] == "rtx" and nv:
            who += [f"{x} open" for x in nv]
        if who:
            out[g["name"]] = "; ".join(sorted(set(who))[:4])
    return out


# ------------------------------------------------------------------ the bisect
class Budget(Exception):
    pass


class Bisect:
    """Group testing over removable groups. released(removed) -> the bits that go idle when
    exactly those groups are off the bus. A bit is assumed held not idle while any of its
    holders is present, so it goes idle once all of them are removed."""

    def __init__(self, names, released, budget=80):
        self.names, self.released, self.budget = list(names), released, budget
        self.holders, self.calls = {}, 0

    def rel(self, removed):
        self.calls += 1
        if self.calls > self.budget:
            raise Budget()
        return set(self.released(frozenset(removed)))

    def run(self, bits):
        """bits: those that go idle with every group removed."""
        self.solve(self.names, frozenset(), set(bits))
        return {b: sorted(h, key=self.names.index) for b, h in self.holders.items()}

    def solve(self, c, z, s):
        if not s:
            return
        if len(c) == 1:
            for b in s:
                self.holders.setdefault(b, set()).add(c[0])
            return
        a, b = c[:len(c) // 2], c[len(c) // 2:]
        sa = self.rel(z | set(a)) & s
        self.solve(a, z, sa)
        rest = s - sa
        if not rest:
            return
        sb = self.rel(z | set(b)) & rest
        self.solve(b, z, sb)
        split = rest - sb
        if split:  # one holder in each half (at least)
            self.solve(b, z | set(a), split)
            self.solve(a, z | set(b), split)


# ------------------------------------------------------------ the quiet phase
def counters():
    """Interrupt counts, per-CPU cpuidle time and usage, context switches (/proc, sysfs)."""
    c = {"mono": time.monotonic(), "irq": {}, "cpuidle": {}, "deepest": None}
    lines = (rd(PROC + "/interrupts", "", 1 << 20) or "").splitlines()
    ncols = len(lines[0].split()) if lines else 0
    for line in lines[1:]:
        f = line.split()
        if not f or not f[0].endswith(":"):
            continue
        counts, rest = [], f[1:]
        while rest and rest[0].isdigit() and len(counts) < ncols:
            counts.append(int(rest.pop(0)))
        key = f[0][:-1]
        label = key if not key.isdigit() else (key + " " + " ".join(rest[-1:]))
        c["irq"][label[:48]] = sum(counts)
    deepest = -1
    for st in glob.glob(SYS + "/devices/system/cpu/cpu[0-9]*/cpuidle/state[0-9]*"):
        cpu, idx = st.split("/")[-3], int(st.rsplit("state", 1)[1])
        name = rd(st + "/name", "?")
        t, u = rd(st + "/time"), rd(st + "/usage")
        if t and t.isdigit():
            c["cpuidle"][(cpu, name)] = (int(t), int(u or 0))
            if idx > deepest:
                deepest, c["deepest"] = idx, name
    for line in (rd(PROC + "/stat", "", 1 << 16) or "").splitlines():
        f = line.split()
        if f and f[0] == "ctxt":
            c["ctxt"] = int(f[1])
    return c


def rates(c0, c1):
    """Wakeups/s (LOC + CAL + RES + device IRQs), the top IRQs, cpuidle residency % per state."""
    dt = c1["mono"] - c0["mono"]
    if dt <= 0:
        return {}
    irq = {k: (v - c0["irq"].get(k, 0)) / dt for k, v in c1["irq"].items()}
    dev = sum(v for k, v in irq.items() if k.split()[0].isdigit())
    per, ncpu = {}, len({k[0] for k in c1["cpuidle"]}) or 1
    for k, (t, u) in c1["cpuidle"].items():
        t0, u0 = c0["cpuidle"].get(k, (t, u))
        a = per.setdefault(k[1], [0.0, 0.0])
        a[0] += (t - t0) / 1e6 / dt / ncpu * 100
        a[1] += (u - u0) / dt
    w = irq.get("LOC", 0) + irq.get("CAL", 0) + irq.get("RES", 0) + dev
    pct = {k: round(v[0], 1) for k, v in per.items()}
    return {"dt": round(dt, 1), "wakeups": round(w), "LOC": round(irq.get("LOC", 0)), "CAL": round(irq.get("CAL", 0)),
            "RES": round(irq.get("RES", 0)), "devirq": round(dev),
            "ctxt": round((c1.get("ctxt", 0) - c0.get("ctxt", 0)) / dt) if "ctxt" in c1 else None,
            "cpuidle_pct": pct, "deepest": c1["deepest"], "deepest_pct": pct.get(c1["deepest"]),
            "top_irq": sorted(((round(v, 1), k) for k, v in irq.items() if v >= 1), reverse=True)[:8]}


# The display -> SMU Z-state decisions (the probes of the #249 kit's snapshot): the DCN's
# messages to the SMU, the Z-state decision at each clock update, and each idle
# optimization allow/disallow with the live Z-state setting and DML StutterPeriod.
PROBE_GROUP = "g16_249b"
PROBES = [
    "f:{g}/smumsg dcn35_smu_send_msg_with_param msg=msg_id:u32 param=param:u32",
    "f:{g}/clk dcn35_update_clocks lower=safe_to_lower:u8 cur=clk_mgr_base->clks.zstate_support:u32 "
    "new=context->bw_ctx.bw.dcn.clk.zstate_support:u32 nstr=context->stream_count:u8",
    "f:{g}/idle dc_allow_idle_optimizations_internal allow=allow:u8 zs=dc->clk_mgr->clks.zstate_support:u32 "
    "nstr=dc->current_state->stream_count:u8 st=dc->current_state->bw_ctx.dml.vba.StutterPeriod:x64",
]
ZS = {0: "UNKNOWN", 1: "ALLOW(Z8+Z9+Z10)", 2: "Z8_ONLY", 3: "Z8_Z10_ONLY", 4: "Z10_ONLY", 5: "DISALLOW"}


class Probes:
    """BTF fprobes in a private tracefs instance; any that the kernel refuses are noted, not fatal."""

    def __init__(self):
        tr = SYS + "/kernel/tracing"
        self.base = tr if os.path.isdir(tr + "/instances") else SYS + "/kernel/debug/tracing"
        self.inst = self.base + "/instances/" + PROBE_GROUP
        self.ok, self.errors = [], []

    def _dyn(self, line):
        fd = os.open(self.base + "/dynamic_events", os.O_WRONLY | os.O_APPEND)
        try:
            os.write(fd, (line + "\n").encode())
        finally:
            os.close(fd)

    def start(self):
        self.stop()
        for p in PROBES:
            line = p.format(g=PROBE_GROUP)
            try:
                self._dyn(line)
                self.ok.append(line.split()[0].split("/")[1])
            except OSError as e:
                self.errors.append(f"{line.split()[0]}: {e}")
        if not self.ok:
            return False
        try:
            os.mkdir(self.inst)
        except FileExistsError:
            pass
        except OSError as e:
            self.errors.append(f"instance: {e}")
            return False
        wr(self.inst + "/buffer_size_kb", 4096)
        for e in self.ok:
            wr(f"{self.inst}/events/{PROBE_GROUP}/{e}/enable", 1)
        wr(self.inst + "/tracing_on", 1)
        return True

    def collect(self):
        wr(self.inst + "/tracing_on", 0)
        return rd(self.inst + "/trace", "", 32 << 20) or ""

    def stop(self):
        if os.path.isdir(self.inst):
            wr(self.inst + "/tracing_on", 0)
            for e in glob.glob(f"{self.inst}/events/{PROBE_GROUP}/*/enable"):
                wr(e, 0)
            try:
                os.rmdir(self.inst)
            except OSError:
                pass
        for e in ("smumsg", "clk", "idle"):
            try:
                self._dyn(f"-:{PROBE_GROUP}/{e}")
            except OSError:
                pass


def summarize_trace(txt, secs):
    """-> report lines, counts."""
    smu, clk, idle, st_vals = {}, {}, {}, []
    for line in txt.splitlines():
        if line.startswith("#"):
            continue
        m = re.search(r" (smumsg|clk|idle): \(.*?\) (.*)$", line) or re.search(r" (smumsg|clk|idle): (.*)$", line)
        if not m:
            continue
        kind, kv = m.group(1), dict(re.findall(r"(\w+)=(\S+)", m.group(2)))
        if kind == "smumsg":
            k = (int(kv.get("msg", "0"), 0), int(kv.get("param", "0"), 0))
            smu[k] = smu.get(k, 0) + 1
        elif kind == "clk":
            k = (kv.get("lower"), kv.get("cur"), kv.get("new"), kv.get("nstr"))
            clk[k] = clk.get(k, 0) + 1
        else:
            k = (kv.get("allow"), kv.get("zs"), kv.get("nstr"))
            idle[k] = idle.get(k, 0) + 1
            try:
                st_vals.append(struct.unpack("<d", struct.pack("<Q", int(kv.get("st", "0"), 16)))[0])
            except (ValueError, struct.error):
                pass

    def zs(v):
        return ZS.get(int(v), v) if v and v.isdigit() else v
    out = [f"display->SMU messages in {secs:g} s: " + (", ".join(f"0x{a:02x}/0x{b:x} x{n}" for (a, b), n in
                                                          sorted(smu.items(), key=lambda x: -x[1])) or "none")]
    out.append("clock updates: " + ("; ".join(f"lower={lo} cur={zs(c)} new={zs(nw)} streams={ns} x{n}" for (lo, c, nw, ns), n in
                                              sorted(clk.items(), key=lambda x: -x[1])) or "none"))
    out.append("idle optimizations: " + ("; ".join(f"allow={a} zstate={zs(z)} streams={ns} x{n}" for (a, z, ns), n in
                                                   sorted(idle.items(), key=lambda x: -x[1])) or "none"))
    if st_vals:
        out.append(f"DML StutterPeriod (us): min {min(st_vals):.0f} median {statistics.median(st_vals):.0f} "
                   f"max {max(st_vals):.0f} (Z8 needs > minimum_z8_residency_time, Z10 > 5000 unless PSR)")
    return out, {"smu": {f"0x{a:02x}/0x{b:x}": n for (a, b), n in smu.items()},
                 "clk": [list(k) + [n] for k, n in clk.items()], "idle": [list(k) + [n] for k, n in idle.items()],
                 "stutter_us": st_vals[:50]}


class Freezer:
    """Freeze the user's app scopes (cgroup v2 freezer) in app.slice: never services, never the
    compositor, the shell, audio, polkit or this kit. What is frozen is listed in a file, so the
    watchdog can thaw it if this process dies."""
    KEEP_COMM = re.compile(r"^(Hyprland|hyprland|quickshell|qs|omarchy-shell|pipewire.*|wireplumber|polkit.*|hyprpolkit.*|"
                           r"xdg-desktop-por.*|uwsm.*|dbus.*|pkexec|systemd.*|g16.*|ssh.*|sshd.*)$")

    def __init__(self, uid, state):
        self.state, self.frozen = state, []
        self.app = f"{SYS}/fs/cgroup/user.slice/user-{uid}.slice/user@{uid}.service/app.slice"
        mine = (rd(PROC + "/self/cgroup") or "").split("::")[-1].strip()
        self.mine = SYS + "/fs/cgroup" + mine

    def units(self):
        out = []
        for root, dirs, _ in os.walk(self.app):
            base = os.path.basename(root)
            if root == self.app:
                continue
            dirs[:] = []
            if not base.endswith(".scope") or base.startswith(("g16", "run-")) or \
                    re.search(r"polkit|portal|keyring|dbus|at-spi|pipewire|wireplumber", base):
                continue
            if self.mine == root or self.mine.startswith(root + "/"):
                continue
            procs = (rd(root + "/cgroup.procs", "", 1 << 16) or "").split()
            comms = {rd(f"{PROC}/{x}/comm", "") for x in procs}
            if not procs or any(self.KEEP_COMM.match(c) for c in comms if c):
                continue
            out.append(root)
        return out

    def apply(self):
        self.frozen = []
        for root in self.units():
            if rd(root + "/cgroup.freeze") == "1":
                continue
            self.frozen.append(root)
            with open(self.state, "w") as f:
                f.write("\n".join(self.frozen) + "\n")
            wr(root + "/cgroup.freeze", 1)
        return len(self.frozen)

    def revert(self):
        n = sum(1 for root in self.frozen if wr(root + "/cgroup.freeze", 0))
        self.frozen = []
        try:
            os.unlink(self.state)
        except OSError:
            pass
        return n


def thaw_from_file(state):
    for root in (rd(state, "", 1 << 16) or "").split():
        wr(root + "/cgroup.freeze", 0)
    try:
        os.unlink(state)
    except OSError:
        pass


# ------------------------------------------------------------------- hardware
class Hw:
    """The G16: groups off and on the bus, the screen, and the readings. All writes go
    through _write, so the offline tests can stand in for the kernel."""

    def __init__(self, groups, state_path, display=None, uid=None):
        self.groups = {g["name"]: g for g in groups}
        self.removed, self.screen_off, self.frozen = frozenset(), False, False
        self.freezer = Freezer(uid, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(state_path), "frozen.txt")) if uid is not None else None
        self.state_path, self.display = state_path, display
        self.state = {"touched": {}, "ports": {}, "screen_off": False, "leds": {}, "done": False}
        self.bat = battery()
        self.amdgpu = next((os.path.realpath(c + "/device") for c in sorted(glob.glob(SYS + "/class/drm/card*"))
                            if re.search(r"card\d+$", c) and card_driver(os.path.basename(c)) == "amdgpu"), None)
        self.rtx = find_rtx(pci_devices())
        self.leds = sorted(glob.glob(SYS + "/class/leds/*kbd_backlight*/brightness"))
        for f in self.leds:
            self.state["leds"][os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(f))] = rd(f)

    # primitives (the tests override these)
    def _write(self, path, value, timeout=30):
        """A sysfs write in a thread: a remove that hangs in the kernel can't hang the run."""
        res = []
        t = threading.Thread(target=lambda: res.append(wr(path, value)), daemon=True)
        t.start()
        t.join(timeout)
        if t.is_alive():
            raise RuntimeError(f"the write to {path} did not return in {timeout} s (a reboot brings the device back)")
        return bool(res and res[0])

    def _exists(self, bdf):
        return os.path.exists(f"{SYS}/bus/pci/devices/{bdf}")

    def _driver(self, bdf):
        p = f"{SYS}/bus/pci/devices/{bdf}/driver"
        return os.path.basename(os.path.realpath(p)) if os.path.lexists(p) else ""

    def sleep(self, s):
        time.sleep(s)

    def save(self):
        self.state["screen_off"] = self.screen_off
        tmp = self.state_path + ".tmp"
        with open(tmp, "w") as f:
            json.dump(self.state, f)
        os.replace(tmp, self.state_path)

    # changes
    def is_on(self, g):
        """On the bus (and, for an unbind group, bound to its driver)."""
        if not self._exists(g["top"]):
            return False
        return g["method"] != "unbind" or self._driver(g["top"]) == g["drivers"][g["top"]]

    def remove(self, g):
        if not self.is_on(g):
            return
        self.state["touched"][g["name"]] = {k: g[k] for k in ("top", "members", "drivers", "method", "bus", "port")}
        self.save()
        if g["method"] == "unbind":
            ok = self._write(f"{SYS}/bus/pci/drivers/{g['drivers'][g['top']]}/unbind", g["top"])
        else:
            ok = self._write(f"{SYS}/bus/pci/devices/{g['top']}/remove", 1)
        if not ok:
            raise RuntimeError(f"taking {g['name']} ({g['top']}) off was refused")
        for _ in range(50):
            if not self.is_on(g):
                return
            self.sleep(0.1)
        raise RuntimeError(f"{g['name']} ({g['top']}) is still there after {g['method']}")

    def rescan(self, names):
        """Bring groups back: rescan each one's bus (never the root bus but for the RTX's
        own port) with its port held awake; bind the unbind groups. Then wait for every
        member and its driver, binding a driver that doesn't come by itself."""
        gs = [self.groups[n] for n in names]
        for g in gs:
            if g["method"] == "unbind" and self._exists(g["top"]) and not self.is_on(g):
                self._write(f"{SYS}/bus/pci/drivers/{g['drivers'][g['top']]}/bind", g["top"])
        gs_bus = [g for g in gs if g["method"] != "unbind"]
        ports = sorted({g["port"] for g in gs_bus if g["port"] and self._exists(g["port"])})
        for p in ports:
            ctl = rd(f"{SYS}/bus/pci/devices/{p}/power/control")
            if ctl and ctl != "on":
                self.state["ports"][p] = ctl
                self.save()
                self._write(f"{SYS}/bus/pci/devices/{p}/power/control", "on")
        for b in sorted({g["bus"] for g in gs_bus}):
            f = f"{SYS}/class/pci_bus/{b}/rescan"
            if not (os.path.exists(f) and self._write(f, 1)):
                self._write(SYS + "/bus/pci/rescan", 1)
        missing = self.wait_back(gs)
        for p in ports:
            if p in self.state["ports"]:
                self._write(f"{SYS}/bus/pci/devices/{p}/power/control", self.state["ports"].pop(p))
        self.save()
        return missing

    def wait_back(self, gs, secs=15):
        want = [(m, g["drivers"].get(m, "")) for g in gs for m in g["members"]]
        t = 0.0
        while t < secs and not all(self._exists(m) for m, _ in want):
            self.sleep(0.25)
            t += 0.25
        for m, drv in want:
            if not drv or not self._exists(m):
                continue
            w = 0.0
            while w < 10 and self._driver(m) != drv:
                self.sleep(0.25)
                w += 0.25
            if self._driver(m) != drv:
                self._write(f"{SYS}/bus/pci/drivers/{drv}/bind", m) or self._write(SYS + "/bus/pci/drivers_probe", m)
        return [m for m, drv in want if not self._exists(m) or (drv and self._driver(m) != drv)]

    def set_state(self, removed, screen_off, frozen=False):
        """Go to exactly these groups removed, this screen state and the apps frozen or not. -> what it did."""
        removed = frozenset(removed)
        info = {"rescanned": [], "removed": [], "missing": [], "screen": None, "frozen": None}
        if self.frozen and not frozen:
            info["frozen"] = f"thawed {self.freezer.revert()}"
            self.frozen = False
        add = self.removed - removed
        if add:
            info["missing"] = self.rescan(sorted(add))
            info["rescanned"] = sorted(add)
            self.removed = self.removed - add
        for n in sorted(removed - self.removed, key=list(self.groups).index):
            self.remove(self.groups[n])
            info["removed"].append(n)
        # A rescan of a shared bus brings back siblings that are to stay removed.
        for n in sorted(removed):
            if self.is_on(self.groups[n]):
                self.remove(self.groups[n])
        self.removed = removed
        if screen_off != self.screen_off and self.display:
            ok = self.display.set(not screen_off)
            info["screen"] = ("off" if screen_off else "on") + ("" if ok else " (not confirmed)")
            self.screen_off = screen_off
            self.save()
        self.leds_off()
        if frozen and not self.frozen and self.freezer:
            info["frozen"] = f"froze {self.freezer.apply()} app scopes"
            self.frozen = True
        return info

    def leds_off(self):
        for f in sorted(glob.glob(SYS + "/class/leds/*kbd_backlight*/brightness")):
            if rd(f) not in ("0", None):
                self._write(f, 0, timeout=5)

    def restore(self):
        """Everything back: the screen, the bus (the global rescan only for what the
        bus rescans missed), the drivers, the keyboard light."""
        errs = []
        if self.frozen:
            self.freezer.revert()
            self.frozen = False
        if self.state.get("probes"):
            Probes().stop()
        if self.screen_off and self.display and not self.display.set(True):
            errs.append("the screen did not come back on (hyprctl): press a key")
        self.screen_off = False
        gs = [n for n in self.state["touched"] if n in self.groups]
        if gs:
            missing = self.rescan(gs)
            if missing:
                self._write(SYS + "/bus/pci/rescan", 1)
                missing = self.wait_back([self.groups[n] for n in gs], secs=10)
            if missing:
                errs.append("not back on the bus or without their driver: " + ", ".join(missing) + " (a reboot brings them back)")
        self.removed = frozenset()
        for name, v in self.state["leds"].items():
            if v is not None:
                self._write(f"{SYS}/class/leds/{name}/brightness", v, timeout=5)
        self.state["done"] = not errs
        self.save()
        return errs

    # readings
    def idlemask(self):
        return parse_mask(rd(SYS + "/kernel/debug/amd_pmc/amd_pmc_idlemask", "", 200))

    def gpu_metrics(self):
        if not self.amdgpu:
            return None
        try:
            with open(self.amdgpu + "/gpu_metrics", "rb") as f:
                return parse_gpu_metrics(f.read())
        except OSError:
            return None

    def sample(self, secs, probes=False):
        """Idlemask at 10 Hz; gpu_metrics every 0.5 s; battery, its status and the RTX every second;
        wakeups and cpuidle over the whole phase; the display -> SMU probes if asked."""
        out = {"masks": [], "gm": [], "bat": [], "status": set(), "rtx": set(), "trace": None}
        pr = None
        if probes:
            self.state["probes"] = True
            self.save()
            pr = Probes()
            if not pr.start():
                out["trace"] = {"lines": ["probes refused: " + "; ".join(pr.errors)], "data": {}}
                pr.stop()
                pr = None
        c0 = counters()
        t0 = time.monotonic()
        k = 0
        while time.monotonic() - t0 < secs:
            out["masks"].append(self.idlemask())
            if k % 5 == 0:
                out["gm"].append(self.gpu_metrics())
            if k % 10 == 0:
                out["bat"].append(bat_w(self.bat))
                out["status"].add(rd(self.bat + "/status") if self.bat else None)
                if self.rtx:
                    out["rtx"].add(rd(f"{SYS}/bus/pci/devices/{self.rtx}/power/runtime_status", "gone"))
            k += 1
            time.sleep(max(0.0, t0 + k * 0.1 - time.monotonic()))
        out["rates"] = rates(c0, counters())
        if pr:
            lines, data = summarize_trace(pr.collect(), secs)
            pr.stop()
            out["trace"] = {"lines": lines + [f"probe refused: {e}" for e in pr.errors], "data": data}
        out["status"], out["rtx"] = sorted(x for x in out["status"] if x), sorted(out["rtx"])
        return out

    def clock(self):
        return time.monotonic()


class Display:
    """DPMS of every output through the user's Hyprland (Lua dispatch first, then the old one)."""

    def __init__(self, user, uid, sig):
        self.base = ["runuser", "-u", user, "--", "env", f"XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/run/user/{uid}",
                     f"HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE={sig}", "hyprctl"]

    def _ctl(self, *a):
        try:
            r = subprocess.run(self.base + list(a), capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10)
            return r.stdout.strip()
        except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
            return ""

    def state_ok(self, on):
        try:
            mons = json.loads(self._ctl("monitors", "-j") or "x")
        except ValueError:
            return None
        return all(bool(m.get("dpmsStatus")) == on for m in mons if not m.get("disabled"))

    def set(self, on):
        """-> True when every output reads back in the wanted state (or, with no read-back,
        when a dispatch said ok)."""
        lua = 'hl.dsp.dpms({ action = "%s" })' % ("enable" if on else "disable")
        said = self._ctl("dispatch", lua) == "ok"
        time.sleep(1)
        got = self.state_ok(on)
        if got is False or (got is None and not said):
            said = self._ctl("dispatch", "dpms", "on" if on else "off") == "ok"
            time.sleep(1)
            got = self.state_ok(on)
        return said if got is None else got


class SimHw:
    """The dry run: devices and bits from a model, a virtual clock, nothing touched."""

    def __init__(self, groups, model, seed=249):
        self.groups = {g["name"]: g for g in groups}
        self.model, self.rng = model, random.Random(seed)
        self.removed, self.screen_off, self.t, self.display, self.frozen = frozenset(), False, 0.0, True, False

    def set_state(self, removed, screen_off, frozen=False):
        removed = frozenset(removed)
        self.frozen = frozen
        add, rem = self.removed - removed, removed - self.removed
        # siblings of a rescanned bus come back and go again
        buses = {self.groups[n]["bus"] for n in add}
        again = {n for n in removed & self.removed if self.groups[n]["bus"] in buses}
        scr = None if screen_off == self.screen_off else ("off" if screen_off else "on")
        self.t += T_RESCAN * bool(add) + T_REMOVE * (len(rem) + len(again)) + T_DPMS * bool(scr)
        self.removed, self.screen_off = removed, screen_off
        return {"rescanned": sorted(add), "removed": sorted(rem | again), "missing": [], "screen": scr,
                "frozen": "froze 12 app scopes (simulated)" if frozen else None}

    def held(self, holders):
        for h in holders:
            if h == "quiet":  # only with everything off, the screen off and the apps frozen
                if not (self.frozen and self.screen_off and self.removed == set(self.groups)):
                    return True
            elif h == "display":
                if not self.screen_off:
                    return True
            elif h not in self.groups or h not in self.removed:
                return True
        return False

    def sample(self, secs, probes=False):
        n = max(1, int(round(secs * 10)))
        base = int(self.model.get("base", "0xffffffff"), 16)
        masks = []
        for _ in range(n):
            m = base
            for b, hs in self.model.get("holders", {}).items():
                m = m & ~(1 << int(b)) if self.held(hs) else m | (1 << int(b))
            for b, p in self.model.get("flicker", {}).items():
                if self.rng.random() < p:
                    m &= ~(1 << int(b))
            masks.append(m)
        w = self.model.get("watts", {})
        saved = sum(w.get(g, 0.0) for g in self.removed) + (w.get("display", 0.0) if self.screen_off else 0.0)
        bat = [w.get("base", 6.5) - saved + self.rng.gauss(0, 0.05) for _ in range(max(1, int(secs)))]
        gm = [{"socket_mw": int((w.get("socket", 4.4) - 0.6 * saved) * 1000), "apu_mw": None, "gfx_mw": 200,
               "core_mw": 200, "dgpu_mw": 0, "ipu_mw": None} for _ in range(max(1, int(secs * 2)))]
        self.t += secs
        quiet = self.frozen and self.screen_off
        r = {"dt": secs, "wakeups": 150 if quiet else 850, "deepest": "C3", "deepest_pct": 99.6 if quiet else 98.4,
             "cpuidle_pct": {"C3": 99.6 if quiet else 98.4}, "top_irq": []}
        tr = {"lines": ["(simulated) idle optimizations: allow=1 zstate=Z8_Z10_ONLY streams=0 x3"], "data": {}} if probes else None
        return {"masks": masks, "gm": gm, "bat": bat, "status": ["Discharging"], "rtx": ["suspended"],
                "rates": r, "trace": tr}

    def sleep(self, s):
        self.t += s

    def clock(self):
        return self.t

    def restore(self):
        self.removed, self.screen_off, self.frozen = frozenset(), False, False
        self.t += T_RESCAN
        return []


DEFAULT_SIM = {
    "_note": "made up for the dry run: not the G16's map",
    "base": "0xffce9add", "flicker": {"7": 0.4},
    "holders": {"1": ["wifi"], "5": ["xhci-kbd"], "8": ["audio", "acp"], "10": ["sd"], "13": ["soc"],
                "14": ["quiet"], "16": ["display"], "20": ["soc"], "21": ["usb4", "xhci-67:00.3"]},
    "watts": {"base": 6.5, "socket": 4.4, "wifi": 0.15, "sd": 0.1, "xhci-kbd": 0.12, "audio": 0.05, "display": 0.8},
}


# ------------------------------------------------------------------- the run
class Abort(Exception):
    pass


def mean(v):
    v = [x for x in v if x is not None]
    return sum(v) / len(v) if v else None


class Runner:
    def __init__(self, hw, groups, args, base_bits=None):
        self.hw, self.args = hw, args
        self.names = [g["name"] for g in groups]
        self.phases, self.cache = [], {}
        self.target = set(base_bits or ())
        self.t0 = hw.clock()

    def measure(self, removed, screen_off=False, why="", secs=None, fresh=False, settle=None, frozen=False, probes=False):
        key = (frozenset(removed), screen_off, frozen)
        if key in self.cache and not fresh:
            return self.cache[key]
        if len(self.phases) >= self.args.max_phases:
            raise Budget()
        info = self.hw.set_state(removed, screen_off, frozen)
        if settle is None:
            settle = self.args.settle_rescan if info["rescanned"] else self.args.settle
        self.hw.sleep(settle)
        s = self.hw.sample(secs or self.args.measure, probes=probes)
        shares = bit_shares(s["masks"])
        hist = {}
        for m in s["masks"]:
            k = f"0x{m:08x}" if m is not None else "unread"
            hist[k] = hist.get(k, 0) + 1
        gm = [g for g in s["gm"] if g]
        p = {"n": len(self.phases) + 1, "why": why, "removed": sorted(key[0], key=self.names.index),
             "screen_off": screen_off, "t": round(self.hw.clock() - self.t0, 1), "settle": settle,
             "change": info, "reads": len(s["masks"]), "masks": dict(sorted(hist.items(), key=lambda x: -x[1])),
             "not_idle": sorted(b for b, v in shares.items() if v >= STUCK),
             "flicker": sorted(b for b, v in shares.items() if IDLE < v < STUCK),
             "shares": {str(b): round(v, 3) for b, v in shares.items() if v > 0},
             "bat_w": mean(s["bat"]), "bat_n": len([x for x in s["bat"] if x is not None]),
             "status": s["status"], "rtx": s["rtx"], "frozen": frozen, "rates": s.get("rates") or {},
             "trace": s.get("trace")}
        for k in ("socket_mw", "apu_mw", "gfx_mw", "core_mw", "dgpu_mw", "ipu_mw"):
            v = mean([g.get(k) for g in gm])
            p[k.replace("_mw", "_w")] = v / 1000 if v is not None else None
        p["valid"] = p["status"] == ["Discharging"]
        p["released"] = sorted(b for b in self.target if shares.get(b, 1.0) <= IDLE)
        self.phases.append(p)
        self.cache[key] = p
        rem = ",".join(p["removed"]) or "-"
        log(f"phase {p['n']:2d} {why:<10} removed={rem}{' screen-off' if screen_off else ''}{' frozen' if frozen else ''} "
            f"not-idle={p['not_idle']} released={p['released']} bat={fmt(p['bat_w'])} W sock={fmt(p['socket_w'])} W "
            f"wakeups={p['rates'].get('wakeups', '-')}/s")
        if info.get("missing"):
            log("  not back after the rescan: " + ", ".join(info["missing"]))
        if not p["valid"]:
            raise Abort(f"the battery is {'/'.join(p['status']) or 'unknown'}: the charger came back")
        return p

    def released(self, removed):
        return set(self.measure(removed, why="bisect")["released"])

    def run(self):
        """Pass 1, the bits (short phases), then pass 2, the watts (long phases)."""
        res = {"holders": {}, "display": [], "internal": [], "unresolved": [], "with_screen": [],
               "verified": {}, "notes": [], "watts": [], "pass1": "run", "quiet_only": []}
        base = self.measure((), why="baseline")
        self.target = set(base["not_idle"])
        base["released"] = []
        res["target"] = sorted(self.target)
        if not self.target:
            res["notes"].append("no bit was not idle at the baseline: nothing to map")
        s_all = set()
        try:
            if self.target:
                # the first split: everything off
                s_all = set(self.measure(self.names, why="all-off")["released"])
                if s_all:
                    bis = Bisect(self.names, self.released, budget=10 ** 6)
                    try:
                        res["holders"] = {str(b): h for b, h in sorted(bis.run(s_all).items())}
                    except Budget:
                        res["holders"] = {str(b): sorted(h, key=self.names.index) for b, h in sorted(bis.holders.items())}
                        raise
                else:
                    res["pass1"] = "skipped: no bit went idle with every removable device off"
                screen = bool(self.args.screen and self.hw.display)
                if screen:
                    res["display"] = self.measure((), True, why="screen-off")["released"]
                    res["with_screen"] = sorted(set(self.measure(self.names, True, why="all+screen")["released"])
                                                - s_all - set(res["display"]))
                # Everything quiet at once, held: every removable device off, the screen off, the
                # app scopes frozen. A bit that goes idle only here wants a quieter machine.
                q = self.measure(self.names, screen, why="quiet", frozen=True, probes=True,
                                 settle=self.args.settle_rescan, secs=self.args.quiet)
                res["quiet_phase"] = q["n"]
                res["quiet_only"] = sorted(set(q["released"]) - s_all - set(res["display"]) - set(res["with_screen"]))
            self.pass2(res)
        except Budget:
            res["notes"].append(f"stopped at {self.args.max_phases} phases: the map is incomplete")
        res["unresolved"] = sorted(s_all - {int(b) for b in res["holders"]})
        res["internal"] = sorted(self.target - s_all - set(res["display"]) - set(res["with_screen"])
                                 - set(res.get("quiet_only", [])))
        return res

    def pass2(self, res):
        """Watts: baseline, everything off, each holder set from pass 1, the baseline again;
        long phases, and each holder set's idlemask confirms pass 1."""
        sets = []
        for b, h in res["holders"].items():
            if tuple(h) not in [x for x, _ in sets]:
                sets.append((tuple(h), []))
            dict(sets)[tuple(h)].append(int(b))
        plan = [("baseline", ()), ("all-off", tuple(self.names))] + [("+".join(h), h) for h, _ in sets] + [("baseline", ())]
        got = []
        for i, (label, rem) in enumerate(plan):
            p = self.measure(rem, why="watts", fresh=True, settle=self.args.watts_settle, secs=self.args.watts_measure,
                             probes=i == 0)  # the first baseline's probes: the quiet phase's comparison
            got.append((label, p))
        for h, bits in sets:
            p = next(p for label, p in got if label == "+".join(h))
            for b in bits:
                res["verified"][str(b)] = b in p["released"]
        bases = [p for label, p in got if label == "baseline"]
        b_bat, b_sock = mean([p["bat_w"] for p in bases]), mean([p["socket_w"] for p in bases])
        bits_of = {"+".join(h): bits for h, bits in sets}
        for label, p in got:
            res["watts"].append({"label": label, "removed": p["removed"], "bits": sorted(bits_of.get(label, [])),
                                 "bat_w": p["bat_w"], "socket_w": p["socket_w"], "phase": p["n"],
                                 "d_bat": None if label == "baseline" else none_sub(p["bat_w"], b_bat),
                                 "d_sock": None if label == "baseline" else none_sub(p["socket_w"], b_sock)})


def fmt(v, f=".2f"):
    return "-" if v is None else format(v, f)


def bits_txt(bits):
    return ", ".join(str(b) for b in bits) if bits else "none"


# ------------------------------------------------------------------- report
def report(res, phases, groups, left, skipped, facts, args, sim=False, minutes=None):
    lab = {g["name"]: f"{g['label']}, {g['top'][5:]}" for g in groups}
    base = [p for p in phases if p["why"] == "baseline"]
    o = ["## idlemask bisect: which devices hold the G16's not-idle bits (#249)", ""]
    if sim:
        o += ["**DRY RUN: simulated devices and bits, not a measurement.**", ""]
    m0 = next(iter(base[0]["masks"])) if base and base[0]["masks"] else "?"
    p1 = [p for p in phases if p["why"] != "watts"]
    p2 = [p for p in phases if p["why"] == "watts"]
    o.append(f"We took the G16's removable PCI devices off the bus in halves (sysfs `remove`, then `rescan`) and read "
             f"amd_pmc's idlemask at 10 Hz after each change: on battery, the RTX runtime-suspended, hands off. "
             f"Kernel {facts.get('kernel', '?')}; {fmt(minutes, '.1f')} min in all. Pass 1 (the bits): {len(p1)} phases, "
             f"{args.settle} s settle ({args.settle_rescan} s after a rescan) and {args.measure} s of reads each"
             + (f" ({res['pass1']})" if res.get("pass1", "run") != "run" else "") + ". Pass 2 (the watts): "
             f"{len(p2)} phases of {args.watts_settle:g} s settle and {args.watts_measure:g} s measured.")
    o.append("")
    o.append(f"Baseline idlemask {m0}: not idle {bits_txt(res.get('target', []))}.")
    o.append("")
    o += ["| bit | held by | confirmed |", "|---|---|---|"]
    for b in res.get("target", []):
        h = res["holders"].get(str(b))
        if h:
            who = (("needs " + " + ".join(lab.get(n, n) for n in h) + " together (no one of them alone lets it go idle)")
                   if len(h) > 1 else lab.get(h[0], h[0]))
            conf = {True: "yes", False: "**no** (did not go idle in pass 2 with only these removed)"}.get(res["verified"].get(str(b)), "-")
        elif b in res["display"]:
            who, conf = "the display: idle with the screen off (DPMS)", "-"
        elif b in res.get("quiet_only", []):
            who, conf = ("idle **only in the quiet phase** (every removable device off, the screen off, the apps "
                         "frozen, held): the machine is otherwise never quiet long enough"), "-"
        elif b in res["with_screen"]:
            who, conf = "idle only with every removable device removed **and** the screen off", "-"
        elif b in res["unresolved"]:
            who, conf = "idle with every removable device removed, but no subset pinned it down (flicker, or a rescan that didn't settle)", "-"
        else:
            who, conf = ("**stuck**: not idle even in the quiet phase (every removable device off, the screen off, "
                         "the apps frozen): firmware or the SoC itself, the NVMe, the AMD GPU or the bridges"), "-"
        o.append(f"| {b} | {who} | {conf} |")
    o.append("")
    q = next((p for p in phases if p["why"] == "quiet"), None)
    if q:
        if res.get("quiet_only"):
            o.append(f"**Quiet:** bits {bits_txt(res['quiet_only'])} go idle only when everything is quiet at once: "
                     "the machine is otherwise never quiet long enough for them.")
        if res.get("internal"):
            o.append(f"**Firmware:** bits {bits_txt(res['internal'])} stay not idle even when everything is quiet at "
                     "once: it isn't a lack of quiet.")
        o.append("")
    if res.get("internal"):
        o.append(f"**For AMD (drm/amd#5863):** bits {bits_txt(res['internal'])} stay not idle with every removable "
                 "device gone, the screen off and the apps frozen. What do they stand for, and what keeps them set?")
        o.append("")
    if q:
        b0 = next((p for p in phases if p["why"] == "watts" and p.get("trace")), base[0] if base else None)
        qr, br = q.get("rates") or {}, (b0 or {}).get("rates") or {}
        o += [f"### Quiet phase (held {args.quiet:g} s)", ""]
        o.append(f"Every removable device off, {'the screen off, ' if q['screen_off'] else 'the screen on (no Hyprland session), '}"
                 f"the app scopes frozen ({q['change'].get('frozen') or 'none'}). Against the baseline (phase {b0['n'] if b0 else '-'}):")
        o.append("")
        o += ["| | quiet | baseline |", "|---|---|---|"]
        o.append(f"| idlemask | {', '.join(f'{k} x{v}' for k, v in list(q['masks'].items())[:2])} | "
                 f"{', '.join(f'{k} x{v}' for k, v in list((b0 or {}).get('masks', {}).items())[:2])} |")
        o.append(f"| not idle | {bits_txt(q['not_idle'])} | {bits_txt((b0 or {}).get('not_idle', []))} |")
        o.append(f"| wakeups/s | {qr.get('wakeups', '-')} | {br.get('wakeups', '-')} |")
        o.append(f"| deepest cpuidle ({qr.get('deepest') or '-'}) residency % | {fmt(qr.get('deepest_pct'), '.1f')} | "
                 f"{fmt(br.get('deepest_pct'), '.1f')} |")
        o.append(f"| socket W | {fmt(q['socket_w'])} | {fmt((b0 or {}).get('socket_w'))} |")
        o.append(f"| battery W | {fmt(q['bat_w'])} | {fmt((b0 or {}).get('bat_w'))} |")
        o.append("")
        for p, name in ((q, "quiet"), (b0, "baseline")):
            if p and p.get("trace"):
                o += [f"Display -> SMU, {name}:", "", "```"] + p["trace"]["lines"] + ["```", ""]
        if qr.get("top_irq"):
            o.append("Top IRQs/s in the quiet phase: " + "; ".join(f"{k} {v}" for v, k in qr["top_irq"]) + ".")
            o.append("")
    if skipped:
        o.append("Not removed: " + "; ".join(f"{n} ({why})" for n, why in skipped.items()) + ".")
        o.append("")
    # watts
    o += ["### Watts (pass 2)", ""]
    if res.get("watts"):
        o += ["Each against the mean of the two baselines.", "",
              "| removed | for bits | battery W | Δ battery W | socket W | Δ socket W |", "|---|---|---|---|---|---|"]
        for w in res["watts"]:
            what = {"baseline": "nothing (baseline)", "all-off": "every removable device"}.get(
                w["label"], " + ".join(w["removed"]))
            o.append(f"| {what} | {bits_txt(w['bits']) if w['bits'] else '-'} | {fmt(w['bat_w'])} | "
                     f"{fmt(w['d_bat'], '+.2f')} | {fmt(w['socket_w'])} | {fmt(w['d_sock'], '+.2f')} |")
        o.append("")
    else:
        o += ["Pass 2 did not run.", ""]
    both = next((p for p in phases if p["why"] == "all+screen"), None)
    if both and base:
        o.append(f"Pass 1, everything removed and the screen off: battery {fmt(both['bat_w'])} W, socket "
                 f"{fmt(both['socket_w'])} W (short phase; baseline {fmt(base[0]['bat_w'])} / {fmt(base[0]['socket_w'])} W).")
    if len(p2) > 1:
        o.append(f"Idlemask at the first and last baseline: {next(iter(p2[0]['masks']), '?')} / "
                 f"{next(iter(p2[-1]['masks']), '?')}.")
    for nt in res.get("notes", []):
        o.append(f"- {nt}")
    o.append("")
    o += ["<details><summary>Every phase</summary>", "", "```"]
    for p in phases:
        masks = ", ".join(f"{k} x{v}" for k, v in list(p["masks"].items())[:3])
        fl = f" flicker={p['flicker']}" if p["flicker"] else ""
        o.append(f"{p['n']:2d} {p['why']:<10} t={p['t']:6.1f}s removed={','.join(p['removed']) or '-'}"
                 f"{' screen-off' if p['screen_off'] else ''}{' frozen' if p.get('frozen') else ''} "
                 f"not-idle={p['not_idle']}{fl} wakeups={(p.get('rates') or {}).get('wakeups', '-')} "
                 f"bat={fmt(p['bat_w'])} sock={fmt(p['socket_w'])} gfx={fmt(p.get('gfx_w'))} core={fmt(p.get('core_w'))} "
                 f"rtx={'/'.join(p['rtx']) or '-'} [{masks}]")
    o += ["```", "", "Groups:", ""]
    for g in groups:
        o.append(f"- {g['name']}: {g['label']} ({', '.join(x[5:] for x in g['members'])})")
    if left:
        o.append("- left alone: " + "; ".join(f"{b[5:]} {w}" for b, w in sorted(left.items())))
    o += ["", "</details>", "", "<sub>bin/g16-idlemask-bisect</sub>"]
    return "\n".join(o) + "\n"


def none_sub(a, b):
    return None if a is None or b is None else a - b


# ------------------------------------------------------------------- stages
def parse(argv):
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="g16-idlemask-bisect", add_help=False)
    ap.add_argument("-h", "--help", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--list", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--post", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--settle", type=float, default=3.0)
    ap.add_argument("--settle-rescan", type=float, default=5.0)
    ap.add_argument("--measure", type=float, default=3.0)
    ap.add_argument("--watts-settle", type=float, default=10.0)
    ap.add_argument("--quiet", type=float, default=60.0)
    ap.add_argument("--watts-measure", type=float, default=30.0)
    ap.add_argument("--max-phases", type=int, default=60)
    ap.add_argument("--skip", default="")
    ap.add_argument("--only", default="")
    ap.add_argument("--no-screen", dest="screen", action="store_false")
    ap.add_argument("--no-follow", dest="follow", action="store_false")
    ap.add_argument("--out", default=None)
    ap.add_argument("--sim", default=None)
    # internal stages
    ap.add_argument("--stage", choices=["detached", "root", "run", "watchdog"], default=None)
    ap.add_argument("--uid", type=int, default=None)
    ap.add_argument("--hypr", default="")
    ap.add_argument("--pid", type=int, default=None)
    a = ap.parse_args(argv)
    if not (0 < a.measure <= 60 and 0 <= a.settle <= 60 and 0 <= a.settle_rescan <= 60 and 1 < a.max_phases <= 200
            and 0 < a.watts_measure <= 300 and 0 <= a.watts_settle <= 120 and 0 < a.quiet <= 300):
        ap.error("--measure, --settle and --settle-rescan are seconds up to 60, --watts-measure up to 300, "
                 "--watts-settle up to 120; --max-phases 2..200")
    if a.hypr and not re.match(r"^[A-Za-z0-9_]+$", a.hypr):
        ap.error("bad --hypr")
    return a


def pass_args(a):
    """The options the later stages need, as arguments."""
    out = ["--settle", str(a.settle), "--settle-rescan", str(a.settle_rescan), "--measure", str(a.measure),
           "--watts-settle", str(a.watts_settle), "--watts-measure", str(a.watts_measure), "--quiet", str(a.quiet),
           "--max-phases", str(a.max_phases), "--out", a.out]
    for k, v in (("--skip", a.skip), ("--only", a.only)):
        if v:
            out += [k, v]
    out += ["--no-screen"] * (not a.screen)
    out += ["--post"] * a.post
    return out


def select(groups, a):
    only = {x for x in a.only.split(",") if x}
    skip = {x for x in a.skip.split(",") if x}
    unknown = (only | skip) - {g["name"] for g in groups}
    if unknown:
        raise SystemExit(f"g16-idlemask-bisect: no such group: {', '.join(sorted(unknown))} "
                         f"(found: {', '.join(g['name'] for g in groups)})")
    keep = [g for g in groups if (not only or g["name"] in only) and g["name"] not in skip]
    return keep, {g["name"]: "--skip" for g in groups if g not in keep}


def kernel():
    return rd(PROC + "/sys/kernel/osrelease", "") or os.uname().release


def show_groups(groups, left, bad, facts):
    print("Removable groups:")
    for g in groups:
        print(f"  {g['name']:<14} {g['label']} ({', '.join(x[5:] for x in g['members'])})")
    print("Left alone: " + ("; ".join(f"{b[5:]} {w}" for b, w in sorted(left.items())) or "nothing"))
    print("Facts: " + ", ".join(f"{k} {v}" for k, v in facts.items()))
    print("Preflight: " + ("ok" if not bad else "would refuse:\n  - " + "\n  - ".join(bad)))


def write_out(out, res, phases, groups, left, skipped, facts, a, sim, minutes):
    os.makedirs(out, exist_ok=True)
    with open(os.path.join(out, "bisect.json"), "w") as f:
        json.dump({"result": res, "phases": phases, "groups": groups, "left": left, "skipped": skipped,
                   "facts": facts, "minutes": minutes, "simulated": sim}, f, indent=1, default=list)
    md = report(res, phases, groups, left, skipped, facts, a, sim=sim, minutes=minutes)
    with open(os.path.join(out, "report.md"), "w") as f:
        f.write(md)
    return md


def stage_dry(a):
    devs = pci_devices()
    groups, left = discover(devs)
    bad, facts = preflight(devs)
    if "GA605" not in facts["machine"]:  # not the G16: its groups as hints, for the simulation only
        left = {}
        groups = [{"name": n, "label": n, "top": t, "members": [t], "drivers": {t: "?"}, "port": "",
                   "bus": t.rsplit(":", 1)[0], "method": "remove"}
                  for n, t in (("wifi", "0000:63:00.0"), ("sd", "0000:62:00.0"), ("usb4", "0000:67:00.5"),
                               ("xhci-kbd", "0000:67:00.0"), ("xhci-cam", "0000:65:00.4"), ("xhci-67:00.3", "0000:67:00.3"),
                               ("xhci-67:00.4", "0000:67:00.4"), ("audio", "0000:65:00.6"), ("hdmi-audio", "0000:65:00.1"),
                               ("acp", "0000:65:00.5"), ("npu", "0000:66:00.1"), ("psp", "0000:65:00.2"), ("smbus", "0000:00:14.0"))]
    groups, skipped = select(groups, a)
    facts["kernel"] = kernel()
    model = DEFAULT_SIM
    if a.sim:
        with open(a.sim) as f:
            model = json.load(f)
    hw = SimHw(groups, model)
    hw.display = a.screen
    r = Runner(hw, groups, a)
    res = r.run()
    hw.restore()
    minutes = (hw.clock() + T_START + T_END) / 60
    out = a.out or os.path.expanduser("~/omarchy-asus-249-bisect-dry")
    write_out(out, res, r.phases, groups, left, skipped, facts, a, True, minutes)
    print(f"dry run: nothing was changed. {len(r.phases)} phases, about {minutes:.1f} min on the G16")
    if bad:
        print("the real run would refuse here:\n  - " + "\n  - ".join(bad))
    print(f"report: {out}/report.md")
    return 0


def hypr_instance():
    """The running Hyprland's instance signature: from the environment, else the newest socket."""
    sig = os.environ.get("HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE", "")
    if re.match(r"^[A-Za-z0-9_]+$", sig):
        return sig
    run = os.environ.get("XDG_RUNTIME_DIR") or f"/run/user/{os.getuid()}"
    socks = [x for x in glob.glob(run + "/hypr/*/.socket.sock")
             if re.match(r"^[A-Za-z0-9_]+$", os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(x)))]
    return os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(max(socks, key=os.path.getmtime))) if socks else ""


def stage_front(a):
    """As the user: preflight, then start the detached unit and follow its log."""
    devs = pci_devices()
    groups, left = discover(devs)
    bad, facts = preflight(devs)
    if a.list:
        show_groups(groups, left, bad, facts)
        return 0
    if bad:
        print("g16-idlemask-bisect: not starting, nothing was changed:\n  - " + "\n  - ".join(bad), file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    select(groups, a)
    if subprocess.run(["systemctl", "--user", "-q", "is-active", UNIT_USER]).returncode == 0:
        print(f"g16-idlemask-bisect: {UNIT_USER} is already running", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    os.makedirs(a.out, exist_ok=True)
    logf = os.path.join(a.out, "run.log")
    open(logf, "w").close()
    env = []
    for k in ("G16_POLKIT_REASON", "G16_ROOT", "SUDO_ASKPASS"):
        if os.environ.get(k):
            env += ["-E", f"{k}={os.environ[k]}"]
    cmd = ["systemd-run", "--user", "-q", "--collect", "-u", UNIT_USER, *env,
           "-p", f"StandardOutput=append:{logf}", "-p", f"StandardError=append:{logf}",
           sys.executable, "-I", SELF, "--stage", "detached", "--hypr", hypr_instance(),
           *pass_args(a)]
    if subprocess.run(cmd).returncode != 0:
        print("g16-idlemask-bisect: could not start the unit", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    print(f"started {UNIT_USER}: approve the root prompt, then hands off (6 to 11 minutes; the keyboard, "
          f"touchpad and Wi-Fi drop out for a while). Log: {logf}")
    if not a.follow:
        return 0
    pos = 0
    while True:
        try:
            with open(logf) as f:
                f.seek(pos)
                chunk = f.read()
                pos = f.tell()
            if chunk:
                print(chunk, end="", flush=True)
        except OSError:
            pass
        if subprocess.run(["systemctl", "--user", "-q", "is-active", UNIT_USER]).returncode != 0:
            break
        time.sleep(1)
    rc = 0 if os.path.exists(os.path.join(a.out, "report.md")) else 1
    print(f"\noutput: {a.out}" if rc == 0 else f"\nno report: see {logf}")
    return rc


def set_stay_awake(on):
    f = os.path.expanduser("~/.local/state/omarchy/indicators/stay-awake")
    have = os.path.exists(f)
    if on == have:
        return False
    try:
        subprocess.run(["omarchy-toggle-idle", "stay-awake" if on else "allow-idle"], capture_output=True, timeout=10)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        pass
    if on and not os.path.exists(f):
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(f), exist_ok=True)
        open(f, "w").close()
    elif not on and os.path.exists(f):
        os.unlink(f)
    return True


def stage_detached(a):
    """The user unit: keep the screen awake, take root once, then post if asked."""
    stay = set_stay_awake(True)
    why = ("G16 idle-power diagnostics (#249): take removable PCI devices off the bus and back, "
           "switch the screen off and freeze the apps for a minute, 6 to 11 minutes in all; everything is put back")
    args = [sys.executable, "-I", SELF, "--stage", "root", "--hypr", a.hypr, *pass_args(a)]
    root = os.environ.get("G16_ROOT", "pkexec")
    if os.environ.get("G16_POLKIT_REASON"):
        cmd = [os.environ["G16_POLKIT_REASON"], "run", why, "--", "pkexec", *args]
    elif root == "sudo":
        cmd = ["sudo"] + (["-A"] if os.environ.get("SUDO_ASKPASS") else []) + args
    else:
        cmd = ["pkexec", "--disable-internal-agent", *args]
    rc = subprocess.run(cmd).returncode
    if stay:
        set_stay_awake(False)
    rep = os.path.join(a.out, "report.md")
    if rc == 0 and a.post and os.path.exists(rep):
        helper = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(SELF), "issue")
        if os.access(helper, os.X_OK):
            r = subprocess.run([helper, "comment", str(ISSUE), "--agent", "laptop-claude", "--body-file", rep])
            print(f"posted to #{ISSUE}" if r.returncode == 0 else f"not posted (bin/issue refused it); the text is in {rep}")
        else:
            print(f"not posted: no bin/issue next to this script; the text is in {rep}")
    return rc


def stage_root(a):
    """Root, from pkexec or sudo: check again, then hand the run to a root transient unit."""
    if os.geteuid() != 0:
        print("g16-idlemask-bisect: the root stage needs root", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    uid = int(os.environ.get("PKEXEC_UID") or os.environ.get("SUDO_UID") or -1)
    try:
        pw = pwd.getpwuid(uid)
    except (KeyError, OverflowError):
        print("g16-idlemask-bisect: can't tell who asked (no PKEXEC_UID/SUDO_UID)", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    out = os.path.realpath(a.out)
    if not out.startswith(pw.pw_dir.rstrip("/") + "/") or os.stat(out).st_uid != uid:
        print("g16-idlemask-bisect: the output directory must be the user's own, in their home", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    bad, _ = preflight(pci_devices(), as_root=True)
    if bad:
        print("g16-idlemask-bisect: not starting, nothing was changed:\n  - " + "\n  - ".join(bad))
        return 1
    if subprocess.run(["systemctl", "-q", "is-active", UNIT_RUN]).returncode == 0:
        print(f"g16-idlemask-bisect: {UNIT_RUN} is already running")
        return 1
    cmd = ["systemd-run", "--wait", "-q", "-P", "--collect", "-u", UNIT_RUN, "-p", "TimeoutStopSec=120",
           sys.executable, "-I", SELF, "--stage", "run", "--uid", str(uid), "--hypr", a.hypr, *pass_args(a)]
    return subprocess.run(cmd).returncode


def start_watchdog(out, deadline):
    cmd = [sys.executable, "-I", SELF, "--stage", "watchdog", "--pid", str(os.getpid()), "--out", out]
    r = subprocess.run(["systemd-run", "-q", "--collect", "-u", f"{UNIT_WATCHDOG}-{os.getpid()}",
                        "-p", f"RuntimeMaxSec={deadline + 300}", *cmd])
    if r.returncode == 0:
        return
    if os.fork() == 0:  # no systemd-run: a child of our own, in its own session
        os.setsid()
        os.execv(sys.executable, cmd)


def load_state(path):
    try:
        with open(path) as f:
            return json.load(f)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return {}


def stage_watchdog(a):
    """Restore when the run is gone without finishing, or stop it after the deadline."""
    state, t0 = os.path.join(a.out, "state.json"), time.monotonic()
    while True:
        time.sleep(2)
        st = load_state(state)
        if st.get("done") or os.path.exists(state + ".finished"):
            return 0
        alive = os.path.exists(f"/proc/{a.pid}")
        if alive and time.monotonic() - t0 < DEADLINE_S:
            continue
        if alive:
            os.kill(a.pid, signal.SIGTERM)
            for _ in range(60):
                time.sleep(1)
                if not os.path.exists(f"/proc/{a.pid}"):
                    break
            else:
                os.kill(a.pid, signal.SIGKILL)
            st = load_state(state)
            if st.get("done") or os.path.exists(state + ".finished"):
                return 0
        restore_from_state(st, a.out)
        return 0


def restore_from_state(st, out):
    """The watchdog's restore: the apps thawed, the probes gone, the screen on, every touched
    device back (its own bus first, the global rescan only when that missed), drivers bound,
    the keyboard light."""
    thaw_from_file(os.path.join(out, "frozen.txt"))
    if st.get("probes"):
        Probes().stop()
    if st.get("screen_off") and st.get("display"):
        d = st["display"]
        Display(d["user"], d["uid"], d["sig"]).set(True)
    touched = list(st.get("touched", {}).values())
    for g in touched:
        top, drv = g.get("top", ""), g.get("drivers", {}).get(g.get("top", ""), "")
        if g.get("method") == "unbind" and drv and not os.path.lexists(f"{SYS}/bus/pci/devices/{top}/driver"):
            wr(f"{SYS}/bus/pci/drivers/{drv}/bind", top)
    for p in st.get("ports", {}):
        wr(f"{SYS}/bus/pci/devices/{p}/power/control", "on")
    for b in sorted({g.get("bus", "") for g in touched if g.get("method") != "unbind"}):
        if not (b and wr(f"{SYS}/class/pci_bus/{b}/rescan", 1)):
            wr(SYS + "/bus/pci/rescan", 1)
    time.sleep(5)
    gone = [m for g in touched for m in g.get("members", []) if not os.path.exists(f"{SYS}/bus/pci/devices/{m}")]
    if gone:
        wr(SYS + "/bus/pci/rescan", 1)
        time.sleep(5)
    for g in touched:
        for m, drv in g.get("drivers", {}).items():
            if drv and os.path.exists(f"{SYS}/bus/pci/devices/{m}") and not os.path.lexists(f"{SYS}/bus/pci/devices/{m}/driver"):
                wr(f"{SYS}/bus/pci/drivers/{drv}/bind", m)
    for p, ctl in st.get("ports", {}).items():
        wr(f"{SYS}/bus/pci/devices/{p}/power/control", ctl)
    for name, v in st.get("leds", {}).items():
        if v is not None:
            wr(f"{SYS}/class/leds/{name}/brightness", v)


def stage_run(a):
    """The root transient unit: the whole run, restore, the report."""
    global LOGF
    out = a.out
    LOGF = os.path.join(out, "controller.log")
    pw = pwd.getpwuid(a.uid)
    signal.signal(signal.SIGPIPE, signal.SIG_IGN)

    def stop(sig, _):
        raise Abort(f"stopped by signal {sig}")
    for s in (signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGINT, signal.SIGHUP):
        signal.signal(s, stop)
    devs = pci_devices()
    bad, facts = preflight(devs, as_root=True)
    if bad:
        log("not starting, nothing was changed: " + "; ".join(bad))
        return 1
    facts["kernel"] = kernel()
    groups, left = discover(devs)
    groups, skipped = select(groups, a)
    for n, why in busy_groups(groups, devs).items():
        skipped[n] = why
    groups = [g for g in groups if g["name"] not in skipped]
    display = None
    if a.screen and a.hypr:
        display = Display(pw.pw_name, a.uid, a.hypr)
    elif a.screen:
        skipped["screen"] = "no Hyprland session"
        a.screen = False
    try:
        os.unlink(os.path.join(out, "state.json.finished"))
    except OSError:
        pass
    hw = Hw(groups, os.path.join(out, "state.json"), display, uid=a.uid)
    if display:
        hw.state["display"] = {"user": pw.pw_name, "uid": a.uid, "sig": a.hypr}
    hw.save()
    start_watchdog(out, DEADLINE_S)
    log(f"groups: {', '.join(g['name'] for g in groups)}; not removed: "
        + ("; ".join(f"{n} ({w})" for n, w in skipped.items()) or "none"))
    r = Runner(hw, groups, a)
    res, rc, err = {"holders": {}, "display": [], "internal": [], "unresolved": [], "with_screen": [],
                    "verified": {}, "notes": [], "target": []}, 0, None
    try:
        res = r.run()
    except (Abort, RuntimeError, Budget) as e:
        err, rc = str(e) or "stopped", 1
        log(f"stopped: {err}")
    finally:
        signal.signal(signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIG_IGN)
        signal.signal(signal.SIGINT, signal.SIG_IGN)
        try:
            errs = hw.restore()
            open(os.path.join(out, "state.json.finished"), "w").close()
        except (RuntimeError, OSError) as e:  # the watchdog tries again once this process is gone
            errs = [f"restore failed: {e}"]
    for e in errs:
        log("RESTORE: " + e)
    if err:
        res.setdefault("notes", []).append(f"the run stopped early: {err}")
    if errs:
        res.setdefault("notes", []).append("after the run: " + "; ".join(errs))
        rc = 1
    minutes = (hw.clock() - r.t0) / 60
    write_out(out, res, r.phases, groups, left, skipped, facts, a, False, minutes)
    for f in os.listdir(out):
        try:
            os.chown(os.path.join(out, f), a.uid, pw.pw_gid)
        except OSError:
            pass
    log(f"done in {minutes:.1f} min: {out}/report.md" + (" (incomplete)" if rc else ""))
    if errs:
        log("a reboot brings every device back")
    return rc


def main(argv):
    a = parse(argv)
    if a.help:
        print(__doc__)
        return 0
    if a.out is None:
        a.out = os.path.expanduser("~/omarchy-asus-249-bisect" + ("-dry" if a.dry_run else ""))
    a.out = os.path.abspath(a.out)
    if a.stage == "detached":
        return stage_detached(a)
    if a.stage == "root":
        return stage_root(a)
    if a.stage == "run":
        return stage_run(a)
    if a.stage == "watchdog":
        return stage_watchdog(a)
    if a.dry_run:
        return stage_dry(a)
    return stage_front(a)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
